{title: When we see Christ}
{subtitle: Hymnal 70}
{x_theme: heaven, joy, prayer}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/When we see Christ.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
It will be worth it all When we see Jesus
Our trials will seem so small When we see Christ
Once glimpse of His dear face All sorrows will erase
And let us run this race Till we see Christ

{comment: Verse 1}
Oft times the day seems long, our trials hard to bear,
We’re tempted to complain, to murmur and despair,
But Christ will soon appear, To catch His bride away,
All tears forever over, In God’s eternal day.

{comment: Verse 2}
Sometimes the sky looks dark, with not a ray of light,
We’re tossed and driven on, No human help in sight,
But there is one in heaven, Who knows our deepest care,
Let Jesus solve your problem, Just go to Him in prayer.

{comment: Verse 3}
Life’s day will soon be over, all stroms forever past,
We’ll cross the great divide to glory safe at last,
We’ll share the joys of heaven, A harp, a home, a crown,
The tempter will be banished, We’ll lay our burdens down.
